     1,
     "Hi Ben,\r<br>\r<br>I think you may need to change out directory you extracted pystan into.  Likely\r<br>Python is trying to import pystan._api from your immediate directory rather\r<br>than from the installed directory.\r<br>\r<br>Best,\r<br>\r<br>Allen\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "\r<br>\r<br>On 07/23, Ben Goodrich wrote:\r<br>&gt; I&#39;m having some trouble. I eventually got python3 versions of all the \r<br>&gt; dependencies installed, which allowed it to build\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; running install_egg_info\r<br>&gt; Writing /usr/local/lib/python3.3/dist-packages/pystan-0.1.1.egg-info\r<br>&gt; running install_clib\r<br>&gt; creating /usr/local/lib/python3.3/dist-packages/pystan/bin\r<br>&gt; copying build/temp.linux-x86_64-3.3/libstan.a -&gt; /usr/local/lib/python3.3/\r<br>&gt; dist-packages/pystan/bin/\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; root@CYBERPOWERPC:/tmp/pystan# updatedb\r<br>&gt; root@CYBERPOWERPC:/tmp/pystan# mlocate -b pystan\r<br>&gt; /usr/local/lib/python3.3/dist-packages/pystan\r<br>&gt; /usr/local/lib/python3.3/dist-packages/pystan-0.1.1.egg-info\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; But it doesn&#39;t work for me when I try it\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; goodrich@CYBERPOWERPC:/tmp/pystan$ python3\r<br>&gt; Python 3.3.2+ (default, Jun 13 2013, 11:56:31) \r<br>&gt; [GCC 4.8.1] on linux\r<br>&gt; Type &quot;help&quot;, &quot;copyright&quot;, &quot;credits&quot; or &quot;license&quot; for more information.\r<br>&gt; &gt;&gt;&gt; import pystan\r<br>&gt; Traceback (most recent call last):\r<br>&gt;   File &quot;&lt;stdin&gt;&quot;, line 1, in &lt;module&gt;\r<br>&gt;   File &quot;./pystan/__init__.py&quot;, line 8, in &lt;module&gt;\r<br>&gt;     from pystan.api import stanc, stan\r<br>&gt;   File &quot;./pystan/api.py&quot;, line 12, in &lt;module&gt;\r<br>&gt;     import pystan._api  # stanc wrapper\r<br>&gt; ImportError: No module named &#39;pystan._api&#39;\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; Ben\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; On Tuesday, July 23, 2013 5:03:11 PM UTC-4, Allen Riddell wrote:\r<br>&gt; &gt;\r<br>&gt; &gt; PyStan 0.1.1 is up on the Python Package Index (Python&#39;s CRAN). \r<br>&gt; &gt;\r<br>&gt; &gt; <a href=\"https://pypi.python.org/pypi/pystan\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://pypi.python.org/pypi/pystan&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792476065101000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3Ews7Hnj9Y-DGTh1YWKwXU\">https://pypi.python.org/pypi/pystan</a> \r<br>&gt; &gt;\r<br>&gt; &gt; Sampling works fine under Python 2.7 and Python 3.3. It&#39;s still alpha \r<br>&gt; &gt; though; \r<br>&gt; &gt; there are a number of things to be implemented, such as reading/writing to \r<br>&gt; &gt; csv. \r<br>&gt; &gt;\r<br>&gt; &gt; Useful links: \r<br>&gt; &gt;\r<br>&gt; &gt; - Source code repo: <a href=\"https://github.com/ariddell/pystan\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/ariddell/pystan&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792476065101000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3-lmRfx7vMw4erCLFbYYj-\">https://github.com/ariddell/pystan</a> \r<br>&gt; &gt; - HTML documentation: <a href=\"http://pystan.readthedocs.org\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://pystan.readthedocs.org&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792476065101000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0NHBLONG8lXNTFnRUba0gX\">http://pystan.readthedocs.org</a> \r<br>&gt; &gt; - Issue tracker: <a href=\"https://github.com/ariddell/pystan/issues\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/ariddell/pystan/issues&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792476065101000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0NOwjQLOPAsqvtkC9m4pjS\">https://github.com/ariddell/pystan/issues</a> \r<br>&gt; &gt;\r<br>\r<br>"
